[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4920381433","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120979#issuecomment-4920381433","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120979","id":4920381433,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJUcP-Q","user":{"login":"Crepestrom","id":179738912,"node_id":"U_kgDOCraZIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/179738912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crepestrom","html_url":"https://github.com/Crepestrom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crepestrom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crepestrom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crepestrom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crepestrom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crepestrom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crepestrom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crepestrom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crepestrom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crepestrom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-09T00:27:12Z","updated_at":"2026-07-09T00:27:12Z","body":"With this pr ray cast bouncing no longer causes issues with inconsistent bounces","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4920381433/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4955558319","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120979#issuecomment-4955558319","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120979","id":4955558319,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJ1_Rrw","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-13T07:37:01Z","updated_at":"2026-07-13T07:57:56Z","body":"I think I see what you are doing, but I don't think you can't just teleport a body backwards like that, because unless I am missing something, you could cause a phantom collision with something behind it. \r\n\r\nImagine that there are two broad phase matches for `body_a` this frame (that is, their swept AABB's overlap, but they don't necessarily collide themselves). There will then be two body_pair entries that are being tested in pre-solve():\r\n\r\n`body_a <- >body_b`\r\n`body_c <-> body_a`\r\n\r\nSo the first body pair `_test_ccd()` finds that `body_a` will hit `body_b`, so it teleports `body_a` backwards immediately. Then the next body pair is tested (in this same frame) and finds that `body_a` now collides with `body_c` (even though `body_c` was well behind `body_a`).\r\n\r\nHowever, your approach did give me an idea that might work. While you can't just change position while the narrow phase is still running, there is a mechanism used by the solver designed for 'positional correction'.\r\n\r\nInstead of subtracting position directly, you can subtract it using biased_linear_velocity, something like below:\r\n```\r\np_A->set_biased_linear_velocity(mnormal * (newlen / p_step) - p_A->get_linear_velocity() + p_A->get_biased_linear_velocity());\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhen velocity integration next runs, it will apply the biased_linear_velocity to the position alongside applying the regular velocity. Then it will set biased_linear_velocity back to zero. This is effectively a way that positional correction can get delayed until after the solve. \r\n\r\nMaybe you could try that approach? (I can't vouch for it without testing it myself, but it's something that could be explored)\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4955558319/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5000640712","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120979#issuecomment-5000640712","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120979","id":5000640712,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKg-4yA","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-17T08:21:19Z","updated_at":"2026-07-17T08:21:19Z","body":"Not sure if you want to explore the fix I suggested. If not, do you mind if I submit a PR with the Biased Velocity based fix? \r\n\r\nI have implemented and am spending some time testing atm.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5000640712/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5011105660","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120979#issuecomment-5011105660","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120979","id":5011105660,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKq9nfA","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-18T11:37:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-18T11:42:32Z","body":"Ok, testing revealed a few more issues and complexities than I hoped. I am kind of wishing I had never looked under this particular rock.\r\n\r\nIt can work to use biased_linear_velocity as I suggested to replace the direct positional teleport, but then you have to be very careful about it because of its other uses. Creating a new positional adjustment vector (purely for this fix) works more cleanly, and would be easier to review and assure, however that just reveals the next problem.\r\n\r\nCCD (as currently implemented) cannot work straight after a collision because the collision changed the motion direction and a new broad phase collision test would be needed. So you can bounce off something and then tunnel right through something else immediately after.\r\n\r\nWhen I do stability tests, 'fixing' the CCD bounce problem makes stability get worse. The lack of bounce was absorbing troubling energy and ensuring that the frame after the bounce didn't need the CCD so much.\r\n\r\nI think fixing (as per your PR) with a safer form of positional adjustment may be valuable for a few games (and maybe worse for others), but there is a better solution that seems tantalisingly close...which is to cast both backwards and forwards in time within the same frame. This would be 4x slower and possibly create time dilation effects that are 2x worse, but then something like CCD could be on all the time and you could safely get high bounce. \r\n\r\nIn the meantime, you could try Godot-rapier-physics. It has its own form of CCD and sub stepping project settings.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5011105660/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/c